From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:33:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] cmake: MinGW-w64 toolchain and third-party support

Build Paddle with MinGW-w64 GCC instead of MSVC:
- take the GNU flag paths (init/flags/configure) for MinGW, build C++ as
  gnu++20 (strict ANSI hides M_PI & co. in the CRT headers), -Wa,-mbig-obj
- keep the MSVC DLL names (common.dll, phi.dll, libpaddle.pyd) by dropping
  the lib prefix, link with lld (resolves dllimport references to symbols
  of the same image like MSVC's LNK4217 behaviour, which Paddle relies on)
- MinGW library names for the bundled zlib/gflags/glog/xxhash/utf8proc/
  warpctc/warprnnt/cryptopp/yaml-cpp/libuv; MSVC-only flags and dirent
  only for MSVC; warpctc's MSVC-only /bigobj /MT; pocketfft has no
  ::aligned_alloc in the Windows CRT (reuse the existing macOS patch)
- LAPACK comes from the system OpenBLAS (no prebuilt download)
- PADDLE_SKIP_SUBMODULE_UPDATE to build from pre-fetched submodules
---
